# Snap the springblades out over and over, with nothing to fight, and let the
# game clock say what a deployment cost.
#
# This is the first half of bd inc-tek.8.8, finding PA-08-F14: the item's page
# says deployment "does require a Handle Device check (DC 15)" and the
# activation handler contained no check at all, so deployment never failed and
# never cost anything.
#
# THE ORACLE IS THE TURN STAMP that posixTerm::DumpScreen writes into every
# dump header (src/Wposix.cpp). Deployment on a passed check still takes no
# time, exactly as the page says. A failed check costs a full round, which the
# engine values at 50 (src/Fight.cpp:2531, a "full round action" in the base
# system). So a jammed attempt moves the stamp and a clean one does not, and
# tools/check_springblade.sh compares consecutive stamps rather than reading a
# message.
#
# There is no monster here on purpose. Combat would move the clock for its own
# reasons and the measurement would stop being about the bracers.

@include springblade-setup.keys

@dump:0001-before
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0002-attempt-1
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0003-attempt-2
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0004-attempt-3
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0005-attempt-4
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0006-attempt-5
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0007-attempt-6
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0008-attempt-7
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0009-attempt-8

@quit
